  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical first step is to establish the simplest possible baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the minimal configuration: single modality, single profile, linear dimensionality reduction, no aggregation or fusion. This tells us whether the RNA signal alone carries sufficient information for the task and provides a performance floor. If it performs well, it raises the bar that more complex multimodal or learned-encoder models must clear; if it underperforms, it motivates exploring learned encoders (scvi, scgpt) or adding the image modality. Choosing the simplest baseline first avoids conflating multiple design choices and gives the cleanest reference point for the remaining 9 experiments."
}

